codex
The decisive install, kill, hard-link, and call-order tests are genuine OS-level models, not purely self-affirming mocks. Two gaps are emerging: pre-install ownership is recorded after `mkdir`/temp creation returns, and the archive test makes `unlink` fail before effect; neither exercises the same “perform, then raise” ambiguity now covered for destination installs. I’m checking whether the mutation driver compensates for either gap.
